      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Inside a glove-box, [(R)-BINOLate]Li (0.721 g, 2.42 mmol) was dissolved in 60 mL of THF and Yb(O3SCF3)3 (0.50 g, 0.806 mmol) was added as a solid in incremental portions. The mixture was stirred for 3 days at room temperature, filtered through dry Celite, and volatiles were removed under vacuum. CH2Cl2 (60 mL) was added, undissolved material was removed by Celite filtration, and the residue was dried, washed once with 2 mL of cold dry diethyl ether and three times with 5 mL of dry hexanes, then dried under reduced pressure to give 1 as a white powder. Pale X-ray quality crystals were obtained by vapor diffusion of dry pentane into a THF solution of 1.",
